id: pm-ts-starter-sdk-toon-codec
title: Use public SDK TOON codecs in generated backend projects
description: Replace generated standalone CLI direct codec dependency with public SDK codecs; preserve certified read-only receipts and document the supported host contract.
type: Chore
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[2]: sdk-adoption,template
created_at: "2026-11-06T18:46:27.416Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-06T19:25:02.777Z"
author: codex-sol
acceptance_criteria: Generated imports and manifests agree on a supported SDK floor; real non-git tracker JSON/TOON round trips preserve representation and source state; regression tests fail on behavioral revert; document SDK codec pattern
comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-06T18:46:39.844Z",codex-sol,"Scope: companion pm-cli-website-25wb and adoption audit S1. Inventory: backend-project.ts generates one direct production encode call and a direct codec manifest dependency; test/backend.test.ts directly decodes the generated CLI output. The package itself has no direct codec dependency. Replace these with public SDK codecs, retain read-only adapter policy and complete-list certification, and verify real non-git tracker output, inertness and generated SDK floor. Companion tracker remains read-only."
  "2026-11-06T18:51:00.094Z",codex-sol,"Public codec exports are present at exact generated floor 2026.10.17; peer range, dev pin and manifest remain aligned without a toolchain bump. Updated generated CLI and test imports to encodeToon/decodeToon from the public SDK, removed the generated direct codec dependency, and documented why application read-only/refusal/certification policy remains. Real non-git npm/Bun consumers and SDK harness pass 13/13 targeted tests. Disposable-copy behavioral reverts: restoring buildBackendProjectFiles alone fails host-owns-codec dependency contract; restoring cliSource alone fails generated build with TS2307 for the unsupported direct codec import. Fixed implementation rerun passes 13/13. Linked-test execution exposed inherited npm_config_allow_scripts causing EALLOWSCRIPTS in nested installs; consumer child environment now removes that setting and npm credential variables."
  "2026-11-06T19:05:49.100Z",codex-sol,"PR #197 is open at d2beea9. Targeted linked test rerun passes 13/13 with zero skips. Local strict health confirms history verification is healthy but reports inherited provenance advisory already tracked by pm-ts-starter-health-legacy-1027 and local extension-host version skew; no history rewrite or duplicate follow-up is needed. Full npm gate is running with a temporary home and disabled global/system Git configuration; Bun follows serially. CI jobs are queued for runners. CodeRabbit review is queued through the required pipeline; automatic skips, trial expiry and reviewer quotas are missing evidence, not approval."
  "2026-11-06T19:24:49.250Z",codex-sol,"Implementation and local acceptance complete: node --test --test-concurrency=1 test/backend.test.ts passes 13/13 with zero skips, including the pm-linked run; npm run lint, npm run typecheck, npm run build:test and changelog check pass. Both isolated behavioral reverts fail and restored implementation passes. Per task instruction CI owns full npm and Bun release:check gates. An extra local npm full-gate attempt was stopped during unrelated compiler-cache tests after passing the generated consumer, crash-recovery and compiler-layout matrices; it is incomplete, not a pass. PR #197 first-head CI passed tracker health, committed-dist checks and CodeQL; full gates remain pending. CodeRabbit is still pending in the shared review queue, with no findings yet and no review approval inferred. External final-head receipts will be retained in the PR body. Existing local health advisories remain covered by pm-ts-starter-health-legacy-1027. No SDK gap or upstream issue was filed; linked npm install environment required clearing inherited allow-scripts as documented above."
files[2]{path,scope}:
  backend-project.ts,project
  test/backend.test.ts,project
tests[1]{command,scope,provenance{author,created_at,source_kind,source_ref}}:
